(ZzzCharacter.cpp:10270-10276). 90 units down the link bone -- knife_gdf, bone 30 -- which is where the staff's skull sits in his fist; BITMAP_SHINY + 1 is Effect/Shiny02.jpg (ZzzOpenData.cpp:5263), at scale 2, in a pale sea-green, and Luminosity is the frame's roll, (rand()%8+2)*0.1 -- a guttering star, as the Chain Scorpion's sting. Drawn by game code, not off this row (as the Chain Scorpion's): play_tuning.h kStarStaffFigure, Play::gatherFolkLights. Two things differ from MU's words. The offset: MU says (0, -90, 0) in its link bone's frame, but the held staff sits on knife_gdf with no turn here and its length is its own +Z (Staff05.glb, the skull at 0.60-0.88 m), so the same 90 units is +Z -- at -Y the star floated a metre off the staff. The light, **ours**: 0.6 of MU's, since Shiny02 peaks at full white and added in HDR it burned to a white star (the user, 2026-09-30: 'too bright and weird'); Shiny02 is 32 texels wide, so Scale 2 is 0.64 m across. A hero holding the Gorgon Staff does not light it yet.
